now more than 180 people have been  killed in devastating flooding and  landslides in nepal and india parts of  the region are experiencing some of the  heaviest post-monsoon rains for years  rescue efforts have begun but the damage  is already immense  like ants drowning in water  that's what houses in the state of  uttarakhand in north india resemble  right now torrential rains and flood  waters have engulfed the region  destroying homes roads and bridges  and killing several people  flooding has also triggered landslides  in one case a home was buried  killing five members of the same family  rescue workers are trying to find the  missing and get people to safety  some have been airlifted  our rescue forces have been split into  multiple smaller teams and have been  deployed to several flood affected areas  on rafts on ropes the national disaster  response force has also deployed teams  we're also clearing several roads that  have been closed due to flood damage  flooding from monsoons is common in  these regions of uttarakhand  but scientists say the problem is made  worse by erratic rains due to climate  change  nearby construction projects are also  adding to the problem  for many their livelihoods have been  completely destroyed  around  the paddy crops of the villagers are  completely damaged and the fields have  washed away the roads are muddy  authorities are visiting the affected  areas with promises to help the most  vulnerable  our government is with the victims  farmers have faced huge losses we are  trying to quickly assess and provide  compensation  neighboring nepal has also been badly  affected  many people have died  residents in remote areas are still  waiting for help as rescue teams  struggle to reach them  but the rains are not stopping  and more is predicted in the coming days
 

